// Phase M — was dead schema (PENDING/SUBMITTED/CONFIRMED/VERIFICATION_FAILED,
// zero supporting code, confirmed in the Phase I discovery pass); redefined
// to the batch lifecycle this phase actually implements. HASHED: evidence
// hashes computed, not yet batched. BATCHED: Merkle root built, evidence
// linked to this anchor row. ANCHORED: a configured external blockchain
// provider confirmed a real transaction. NOT_CONFIGURED: no provider is
// configured — the batch/Merkle/hash work is still real and persisted,
// only the external anchor step was skipped, honestly. FAILED: a
// configured provider was attempted and it failed.
enum BlockchainAnchorStatus {
  HASHED
  BATCHED
  ANCHORED
  NOT_CONFIGURED
  FAILED
}

enum AlertSeverity {
